Twelve Alltag scenarios, and fix the cookie every learner shared

userFromCookie() read dm_user, which sign-in stopped writing when it moved
to dm_uid. Every learner fell back to DEFAULT_USER and shared one set of
localStorage buckets: cached plan, resume offer, tour flag, and the queue
of answers given offline. Invisible on an install where the signed-in id
equals the fallback, which is exactly where it was written.

Six more Alltag scenarios (twelve total). content.test.mts asserted
survival.length === 6, so adding any would have failed it; it now checks
the floor and that no two scenarios share an id.

Comments compressed in config, trust, who, secrets, apikey and
shared-cache, keeping the load-bearing ones to a line.

